// An array of promises is not a promise. (The reverse -- a promise is not an
// array of promises -- is bad_promise_not_array.lpc; a fail fixture can only
// pin one diagnostic.) Note the array literal here types as `mixed *`, so
// the rejection is `promise<int> vs mixed *`: what this pins is that a
// promise declaration does not accept an array, not anything about the
// element type.
async int f() { return 1; }
void g() {
  promise<int> p = ({ f() });
}
